[TITLE]
Tiny water distribution network - OSP proof of concept

; Lines starting with a semicolon are comments.
; With Units LPS, junction demands are in litres/second,
; pipe lengths and elevations are in metres, and diameters are in mm.
;
; CHANGES FROM THE FIRST VERSION (made so leaks produce measurable pressure changes):
;   1. Every base demand multiplied by 6 (e.g. J1 0.5 -> 3.0 L/s).
;   2. Diameters reduced: P1 250->200, P2 and P3 200->150, P4 to P7 150->100 mm.
;   Reason: with the original oversized pipes a 10 mm leak changed pressure by < 0.1 m,
;   so no sensor could ever alarm. These are illustrative values, NOT measured utility data.
;   Time steps changed to 5 minutes so detection timing has useful resolution.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elevation   BaseDemand   Pattern
J1    20          3.0          DAILY
J2    18          4.2          DAILY
J3    16          3.6          DAILY
J4    15          4.8          DAILY
J5    14          3.0          DAILY
J6    13          2.4          DAILY

[RESERVOIRS]
; R1 supplies water at a fixed total hydraulic head of 50 m.
;ID   Head
R1    50

[PIPES]
;ID   Start  End   Length  Diameter  Roughness  MinorLoss  Status
P1    R1     J1    300     200       120        0          OPEN
P2    J1     J2    250     150       120        0          OPEN
P3    J2     J3    250     150       120        0          OPEN
P4    J3     J4    250     100       120        0          OPEN
P5    J4     J5    250     100       120        0          OPEN
P6    J5     J6    250     100       120        0          OPEN
P7    J2     J4    350     100       120        0          OPEN

[PATTERNS]
; Eight demand multipliers, each lasting three hours.
; This is an illustrative pattern, not measured utility data.
; Hours:  0-3  3-6  6-9  9-12  12-15  15-18  18-21  21-24
DAILY     0.6  0.7  1.4  1.1   1.0    1.2    1.5    0.8

[OPTIONS]
Units      LPS
Headloss   H-W
Quality    NONE

[TIMES]
Duration             24:00
Hydraulic Timestep    0:05
Pattern Timestep      3:00
Report Timestep       0:05

[REPORT]
Status     NO
Summary    YES

[COORDINATES]
; Coordinates are for drawing the network, not computing pipe lengths.
;Node   X     Y
R1      0     50
J1      10    40
J2      20    30
J3      30    20
J4      30    35
J5      40    25
J6      50    15

[END]
